  "brief": "Long, low gable-roofed stock barn: a chest-high base of whitewashed rough limestone blocks carrying a frame upper storey of weathered vertical boards patched with strips of corrugated steel, under a standing-seam metal roof. The gable end facing the yard has a projecting hay hood over the loft door and a wagon door below; plank stable doors along the long side open to wooden feedlot pens. (Entry is at the gable end, not the side; builder should treat it as a three-bay barn turned end-on.)",
